about a future state. The act of declaring is 已发生, the state of not being his assistant is future (or present but newly established).\n\nActually, if I say \"从今天起我不再做X\" - I'm announcing that starting today, I won't do X. The \"从今天起\" part is the time reference. The \"我不再做X\" is the future state. So it's a 计划.\n\nAlternatively, since she's already giving back the badge (the symbol of her role), the role change is happening in real-time. So the state change to \"not being his assistant\" is 已发生. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about this more carefully. She says \"从今天起我不再做助理\" and simultaneously gives back the badge. These are part of the same action sequence. The badge return is the symbolic act of quitting. The statement is the verbal confirmation. Together they form the act of ending the assistant relationship.\n\nI think the cleanest recording is:\n- Fact: 乔米对褚衡说\"从今天起，我不再给你做助理\" (已发生, speech event)\n- Fact: 乔米从今天起不再担任褚衡的助理 (the content - 计划, since she states it's from today going forward, or 已发生 since the badge handover is happening)\n\nI'll go with 计划 for the content, as it's her stated future state.\n\nActually, let me re-read the instruction: \"已经说出口的询问、请求、命令、劝说、建议和评价，本身都按已经发生的言语事件记录；说话内容不能因此升级成客观事实。\"\n\nSo 询问, 请求, 命令, 劝说, 建议, 评价 are all 已发生 as speech events. But 计划 or 承诺 (about the speaker's own future action) - the content is the speaker's plan/commitment. \n\nHer statement \"我不再给你做助理\" is a declaration/intent about her own future action. This could be:\n- A 计划 (her plan)\n- A 承诺 (her commitment)\n\nShe says \"我不再给你做助理\" - \"I will no longer be your assistant.\" This is her own decision/commitment. It's 承诺 (since she's declaring her own commitment to no longer be the assistant). Or 计划 (since she's stating her plan).\n\nActually, I think the cleanest is to record just the speech event and mark the content as the subject of the speech. The content is about her own action, so it's 计划 (her stated plan to no longer be the assistant).\n\nLet me also think: 褚衡没有把工牌还回去 - is this a negation? Yes, \"没有\" is a negation. The fact is that he didn't return the badge. Status: 否定.\n\nOK, let me write the final JSON.\n\nWait, one more consideration: \"工位夹\" - workstation clip. This is a detail about the workspace. The fact that the badge was on a clip at her workstation implies she has a workstation. I could record this but it's a minor detail.\n\nLet me also consider: 褚衡 \"把卡片翻过去\" - \"flipped the card over.\" This is an action with the badge. The \"卡片\" refers to the work badge (工牌) which is card-shaped. So he's flipping the badge to its other side. This is recorded as fact #7.\n\n\"伸手把两人中间那条一直共用的抽屉锁上\" - he reached out and locked the shared drawer. The \"伸手\" detail shows his deliberate action. The \"一直共用的\" shows the long-term sharing. Recorded as fact #8.\n\n\"乔米站在原处看了他两秒\" - she stood and looked at him for two seconds. Recorded as fact #9.\n\n\"把桌上那支共用的红笔也推进抽屉缝\" - she pushed the shared red pen from the table into the drawer gap. Recorded as fact #10.\n\n\"转身走了\" - she turned and left. Recorded as fact #11.\n\nOK let me write it out:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"facts\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"乔米从工位夹上摘下工牌\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"乔米把工牌从工位夹上摘下来\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"乔米把工牌塞进褚衡摊开的掌心\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"塞进褚衡摊开的掌心\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"乔米对褚衡说'从今天起，我不再给你做助理'\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"speaker\": \"乔米\",\n      \"evidence\": \"说：'从今天起，我不再给你做助理。'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"乔米声称从今天起不再做褚衡的助理\",\n      \"status\": \"计划\",\n      \"speaker\": \"乔米\",\n      \"evidence\": \"'从今天起，我不再给你做助理。'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"乔米此前是褚衡的助理\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"我不再给你做助理\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"褚衡没有把工牌还给乔米\",\n      \"status\": \"否定\",\n      \"evidence\": \"褚衡没有把工牌还回去\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"褚衡把工牌卡片翻过去\",\n      \"status\": \"已发生\",\n      \"evidence\": \"只把卡片翻过去\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact